# radroots_net

`radroots_net` is a private, publication-frozen compatibility package for the
superseded broad network/runtime layer. New consumers and new behavior are
forbidden. Final transport contracts belong to `radroots_transport`, shared
orchestration belongs to `radroots_sync`, and application composition belongs
to `radroots_sdk` or the host.

## Compatibility quarantine

The existing `app_rt` consumer still resolves this package as
`radroots_net_core` while its downstream cutover is pending. Removing the
package now would break that standalone consumer, so `RCRV1-DEV-010` retains
only this documentation-hidden, `publish = false` bridge. Step 313 removes the
package after the first-party consumer matrix proves the cutover complete.

Do not add consumers, features, public contracts, transport implementations,
or runtime behavior here. In particular, the optional legacy Nostr-client
surface is not the public `radroots_transport_nostr` API and cannot enter a
release feature closure.

